  <h2 id="how-to-use">How to use Ginseng</h2>
  <h3>Recommended daily dose</h3>
  <p>
    For standardised Panax ginseng root extract, most clinical studies and traditional references suggest <strong>200 mg to 400 mg per day</strong> for adults, taken with food. Some traditional formulas use higher amounts — always follow the directions on your specific product.
  </p>
  <h3>Cycling Ginseng</h3>
  <p>
    Many traditional and modern practitioners recommend taking Ginseng in <strong>cycles of 8 to 12 weeks on, followed by 2 to 4 weeks off</strong>. This approach is widely used in herbal medicine for tonics and may help maintain the body's responsiveness to the herb over time.
  </p>
  <h3>How to choose a good Ginseng product</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Look for <strong>standardised root extract</strong>, with the percentage of ginsenosides clearly stated.</li>
    <li>Choose roots aged at least 4–6 years where specified.</li>
    <li>Pick a format that suits your routine — capsules, instant beverage or coffee blend.</li>
    <li>Choose a manufacturer with documented quality controls.</li>
  </ul>

  <figure>
